WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.537
Part B turns to SailPoint and Graph.

2
00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:06.350
Step six runs the SailPoint
client tests: four pass.

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:10.091
Step seven lists what the drift
client needs from SailPoint:

4
00:00:10.091 --> 00:00:11.962
search read and accounts read.

5
00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:15.471
Step eight catches a manage
scope on that read client:

6
00:00:15.471 --> 00:00:19.138
nothing missing, accounts
manage extra, and it exits one.

7
00:00:19.138 --> 00:00:23.199
Step nine checks the drift client's
scopes against the workflow task.

8
00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:27.100
The workflow scope is missing,
and both read scopes are extra.

9
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.812
That's the point of the step:
the two jobs need two clients.

10
00:00:30.812 --> 00:00:34.237
Step ten checks the Graph
app registration twice.

11
00:00:34.237 --> 00:00:39.312
For a drift run that reads the audit,
AuditLog dot Read dot All is missing.

12
00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:43.533
With the required-only option, for
a run that doesn't read the audit,

13
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:46.800
least privilege holds, and
the command exits zero.
